# 👤 Tiny Player System

## 👤 Tiny Players

Tiny Players experience the Giant at a completely different scale. Their small size is a gameplay advantage as well as a challenge.

## 🧰 Gadgets & Temporary Upgrades

Frozen Giant Showdown established a temporary upgrade system that fits GIANTBOUND well. These upgrades should help Tiny Players survive, move, and counter Giant pressure without becoming permanent pay-to-win advantages.

### 🛠️ Adapted Upgrade Pool

- 🪖 Helmet — improves protection against hazards.
- 👢 Speed Boots — temporarily improves movement speed.
- 🦘 Double Jump — adds an extra jump for traversal.
- 🛡️ Shield — provides temporary protection.
- 🎯 Better Aim — improves accuracy with ranged/objective tools when a mode uses them.
- 🔄 Faster Reload — reduces reload time for compatible tools.

The exact effects can change depending on the final game mode.

## 🎁 Lucky Items

A limited lucky-item system can appear during a match. Rewards may include temporary movement boosts, shields, extra jumps, or other short-term advantages.

Lucky items should create exciting moments without deciding the whole match by themselves.

## 🧗 Movement & Parkour

The Frozen Giant Showdown parkour system provides the starting movement pool for GIANTBOUND:

- 🧊 Moving Platforms
- 💥 Breaking Bridges
- 🧊 Slippery Surfaces
- 🔄 Rotating Platforms
- ⛷️ Jump Pads
- 🧱 Environmental Obstacles

GIANTBOUND can move beyond frozen/ice visuals and reuse the same gameplay ideas in different environments.

## ❤️ Respawn Baseline

The original game used a non-elimination fall system: falling from the parkour area caused a short respawn at the start instead of removing the player from the match.

GIANTBOUND can use this as the initial baseline, with the exact respawn time and conditions to be tested.

## 🎯 Design Goal

Tiny Players should feel clever and capable, not simply weak because they are small. Their advantage comes from movement, scale, teamwork, gadgets, and finding routes around the Giant's actions.

